--- !u!114 &6008010203184604818
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 5736024292224911486}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 1154532148a7a41d5818123ea6f7d5b6, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  lectureSpot: {x: 3.2, y: 0.15, z: 10}
  lectureFacingYaw: 180
  boardSpot: {x: 3.6, y: 0.15, z: 11.3}
  boardFacingYaw: 0
  roomRect: {x: 0.4, y: 0.5, z: 9.6, w: 11.4}
  lectureTime: {x: 7, y: 11}
  boardTime: {x: 5, y: 8}
  lookAroundTime: {x: 2, y: 4}
  lectureWeight: 0.5
  boardWeight: 0.3
  lines:
  - text: Today we continue with the Founding Charter of our school.
  - text: Our school was founded in 1952. Nineteen fifty-two. Far away from the noise
      of the city.
  - text: 'The Charter has four rules. Rule one: what is seen, is safe.'
  - text: Every device in this building is monitored. That is how we keep you safe.
  - text: 'Rule two: no voice leaves these walls.'
  - text: 'Rule three: lights out is at nine. Twenty-one hundred. Exactly.'
  - text: The pigeons in the courtyard are not monitored. ...Yet.
  - text: The founder planted the oak tree in the courtyard on the very first day.
  - text: Seven classes. Seven bells. Every single day.
  - text: 'Whoever drew a moustache on the founder''s portrait: I know you are left-handed.'
  - text: 'Rule four: we do not keep things from each other.'
  - text: A quiet room is a good room. Remember that.
  - text: And the back row, by the window... I sat in that seat once. Before you.
      Before all of you.
  questions:
  - aboutLine: -1
    question: What is six plus seven?
    options:
    - 11
    - 13
    - 15
    correct: 1
  - aboutLine: 1
    question: In what year was our school founded?
    options:
    - 1925
    - 1962
    - 1952
    correct: 2
  - aboutLine: 2
    question: What is Rule one of the Charter?
    options:
    - What is seen, is safe
    - Silence is golden
    - Hands on the desk
    correct: 0
  - aboutLine: 5
    question: When is lights out?
    options:
    - 22:00
    - 21:00
    - 20:00
    correct: 1
  - aboutLine: 7
    question: What did the founder plant in the courtyard?
    options:
    - An oak tree
    - A pine tree
    - A rose garden
    correct: 0
  - aboutLine: 8
    question: How many bells ring every day?
    options:
    - Five
    - Nine
    - Seven
    correct: 2
  - aboutLine: 4
    question: What is Rule two?
    options:
    - No voice leaves these walls
    - No running in the halls
    - No phones after nine
    correct: 0
  - aboutLine: 6
    question: Which of these is NOT monitored?
    options:
    - The library
    - The courtyard pigeons
    - The hallway
    correct: 1
